{"study_accession":"PRJNA759244","secondary_study_accession":"SRP335061","title":"Integrating whole blood transcriptomic collection procedures into the current anti-doping testing system, including long-term storage and re-testing of anti-doping samples [Short-term]","description":"Purpose: Recombinant human erythropoietin administration studies involving “omics” approaches have demonstrated a gene-expression signature that could aid detection of blood doping. However, current anti-doping testing does not involve blood collection into tubes with RNA preservative. This study investigated if whole blood in short-term storage could be used for transcriptomic analysis despite lacking RNA preservation. Methods: Whole blood samples were collected from fourteen male healthy individuals. Short-term storage: whole blood collected into K2EDTA tubes and subjected to short-term (i.e., at 4°C) storage for 6 hours, 12 hours, 24 hours and 48 hours. After storage, blood from K2EDTA tubes were transferred into Tempus™ Blood tubes, and then extracted using Tempus™ Spin RNA Isolation Kit (Life Technologies, Carlsbad, CA, USA). Samples from four subjects of each time point that presented higher RIN value (≥7) were selected for RNA_Seq analysis. Results: The experiment provided RNA quality and purity for gene expression analysis. Considering 6-hours storage as a reference group, the number of differentially expressed genes were 19, 45 and 70 in comparison to 12, 24 and 48-hours, respectively (which means 0.37, 0.88 and 1.37% of mapped genes). Of the 19 differentially expressed genes in the comparison 6 vs. 12-hours, 9 overlapped with the 45 in the comparison 12 vs. 24-hours. Furthermore, 40 of those 45 overlapped with the 70 differentially expressed in the comparison 6 vs. 48-hours. None of the transcripts described in previous studies (Durussel et al. 2016; Wang, Durussel, et al. 2017) were differently expressed. Conclusion: RNA quantity, purity and integrity was not significantly compromised from short-term storage in blood storage tubes lacking RNA stabilisation, indicating that transcriptomic/omics analysis could be conducted using anti-doping samples collected without RNA preservation. Overall design: Blood samples were collected using K2EDTA tubes and stored at 4C for 6, 12, 24 and 48 hours. After short-term storage, blood samples from K2EDTA tubes were transferred into Tempus tube and extracted by using Tempus™ Spin RNA Isolation Kit. The different gene expression between groups was compared.","pubmed":"34765642","geo_series":"","n_samples":16,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21160532","study_accession":"PRJNA759244","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"12 hours (6_12.1)","description":"12 hours (6_12.1)","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5551665","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-09-05","attributes":[["source_name","Healthy male"],["tissue","Whole blood"],["sex","male"],["group","EDTA"],["time","short-term storage (12 hours)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR15680323","experiment_accession":"SRX11976679","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"DNBSEQ-G400","read_count":210873492,"base_count":21087349200,"first_public":"2021-09-05","experiment_title":"DNBSEQ-G400 sequencing: GSM5551665: 12 hours (6_12.1) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN21160533","study_accession":"PRJNA759244","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"6 hours (9_6.1)","description":"6 hours (9_6.1)","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5551666","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-09-05","attributes":[["source_name","Healthy male"],["tissue","Whole blood"],["sex","male"],["group","EDTA"],["time","short-term storage (6 hours)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR15680324","experiment_accession":"SRX11976680","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"DNBSEQ-G400","read_count":